{"step_index":92,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-13T19:04:41Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-14T00:34:41+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-14T00:34:41+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/renu5/.gemini/antigravity/brain/8ea3dee6-cf9c-4ba2-88dc-0b3551467a06/.system_generated/steps/90/content.md`\nTotal Lines: 82\nTotal Bytes: 4850\nShowing lines 1 to 82\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: Description: If you sell or give away your device, you may be able to transfer your AppleCare plan to the new owner.\n2: \n3: Source: https://support.apple.com/en-in/111801\n4: \n5: ---\n6: \n7: - [Apple](https://www.apple.com/in/)\n8: - [Store](https://www.apple.com/in/shop/goto/store)[Mac](https://www.apple.com/in/mac/)[iPad](https://www.apple.com/in/ipad/)[iPhone](https://www.apple.com/in/iphone/)[Watch](https://www.apple.com/in/watch/)[AirPods](https://www.apple.com/in/airpods/)[TV & Home](https://www.apple.com/in/tv-home/)[Entertainment](https://www.apple.com/in/entertainment/)[Accessories](https://www.apple.com/in/shop/goto/buy_accessories)[Support](https://support.apple.com/en-in/?cid=gn-ols-home-hp-tab)\n9: - [Store](https://www.apple.com/in/shop/goto/store)\n10: - [Mac](https://www.apple.com/in/mac/)\n11: - [iPad](https://www.apple.com/in/ipad/)\n12: - [iPhone](https://www.apple.com/in/iphone/)\n13: - [Watch](https://www.apple.com/in/watch/)\n14: - [AirPods](https://www.apple.com/in/airpods/)\n15: - [TV & Home](https://www.apple.com/in/tv-home/)\n16: - [Entertainment](https://www.apple.com/in/entertainment/)\n17: - [Accessories](https://www.apple.com/in/shop/goto/buy_accessories)\n18: - [Support](https://support.apple.com/en-in/?cid=gn-ols-home-hp-tab)\n19: - https://support.apple.com/kb/index?page=search&locale=en_IN\n20: - [0+](https://www.apple.com/in/shop/goto/bag)\n21: [Apple](https://www.apple.com/in/)\n22: - [Store](https://www.apple.com/in/shop/goto/store)\n23: [Store](https://www.apple.com/in/shop/goto/store)\n2\n<truncated 1669 bytes>\nare agreement number, the serial number of the device and the proof of coverage for the AppleCare plan.\n51: Find the original sales receipt for the device.\n52: Get the new owner’s name, address, email address and phone number.\n53: [Contact Apple Support](https://getsupport.apple.com/?caller=kbase&PGF=PGF66001&category_id=SC0089&symptom_id=20455).\n54: For some AppleCare plan types, and in some countries or regions, you may not be able to transfer an AppleCare plan to a new owner. For details, [review the applicable AppleCare Terms and Conditions](https://www.apple.com/uk/legal/sales-support/). If you’re not sure which plan you have, [check your coverage](https://checkcoverage.apple.com).\n55: \n56: If you make monthly or annual payments* for your AppleCare plan and your plan is already linked to an Apple Account, then it can’t be transferred to a new owner.\n57: * In some countries and regions, you may have the option to pay monthly or annually for your AppleCare plan. This option is not available for all AppleCare plans or all countries and regions.\n58: \n59: ## If you receive a replacement device\n60: If we replace your device instead of repairing it, we’ll automatically transfer your plan to your new device. If transfer of coverage isn’t possible, we’ll offer other options.\n61: \n62: ## Apple Footer\n63: [\n64:                     Apple](https://www.apple.com/in)\n65: 1. \n66: \n67:                                 [Support](https://support.apple.com/en-in)\n68: \n69: \n70: \n71: 2. \n72:                             Transfer your AppleCare plan\n73: \n74: \n75: [Support](https://support.apple.com/en-in)\n76: [India](https://support.apple.com/en-in/111801/localeselector)\n77: [Privacy Policy](https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/en-ww/)\n78: [Terms of Use](https://www.apple.com/in/legal/internet-services/)\n79: [Sales Policy](https://www.apple.com/in/shop/browse/open/salespolicies)\n80: [Site Map](https://www.apple.com/in/sitemap/)\n81: \n82: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
{"step_index":93,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-13T19:04:41Z","thinking":"Apple Certified Refurbished Macs are eligible for AppleCare+ like new products, indicated by the standard warranty and support. A potential exception may exist for India, requiring further investigation to clarify current operational limitations.\n\n\nIf an Apple Certified Refurbished Mac is purchased abroad by an Indian customer, AppleCare+ can be added within 60 days of the original purchase. Mac warranties and AppleCare+ are global, so service in India is available at Apple Stores or authorized providers.\n\nAppleCare+ eligibility is tied to the original purchase date (within 60 days), not the second-hand sale date. Therefore, purchasing AppleCare+ for a used Mac is only possible if it's within the original 60-day window from the initial purchase, regardless of the third-party seller.\n\n\nExamining the constraints, a second-hand Mac older than 60 days from its original purchase date is ineligible for new AppleCare+ in India, due to the lack of an inspection-to-buy program. However, an existing upfront AppleCare+ plan tied to the Mac's serial number transfers automatically or can be formally transferred with the original invoice. Conversely, a monthly/annual subscription plan linked to an Apple Account cannot be transferred.\n\nThe time limit for purchasing AppleCare+ after buying a Mac is 60 days from the purchase date in most cases, but needs confirmation in India, though the notes show that it is currently 60 days.\n\n\nExamining the official support page, AppleCare+ can be added within 60 days of a new purchase, with variations for refurbished and second-hand Macs. Confirmed that pricing for MacBook Pro in India is available, differentiating between 14-inch and 16-inch models, both upfront and monthly. A standard 1-year warranty covers manufacturing defects.\n\n\nInitial assessment indicates that standard warranty does not cover accidental damage or normal battery degradation, but provides 90 days of technical support. AppleCare+ extends coverage to three years, or indefinitely with renewals, and covers accidental damage with deductibles for screen/enclosure damage and other ADH incidents. AppleCare+ offers free battery replacement if capacity falls below 80% of original.\n\n\nThe 60-day window for AppleCare+ purchase starts from the original Mac purchase date, not the second-hand purchase date; this is the primary restriction. An Apple Certified Refurbished store is not available in India, so third-party refurbished Macs may not be covered. To enroll, the used Mac must pass remote diagnostics or physical inspection and cannot have pre-existing damage or unauthorized repairs.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"read_url_content","args":{"Url":"\"https://www.apple.com/legal/sales-support/applecare/appmacin.html\"","toolAction":"\"Checking AppleCare Mac India legal terms\"","toolSummary":"\"AppleCare Mac India legal terms\""}}]}
